WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.580
It's a new trading day. Welcome to Modern Investing Techniques, episode 56 for May 28th,

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:07.320
2026.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:13.220
I'm Patrick, coming to you from Vancouver. Here's your daily market intelligence and

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:14.520
today's practice trade.

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:20.820
Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:26.620
investment of the day uses simulated trades with no real money. I'm not a licensed financial

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:31.620
advisor, and this is in financial advice. Always do your own research before putting

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:37.660
real money to work. Oil prices jumping over 2% on renewed iron tensions means Canadian

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:44.960
energy exposure in a TFSA could face sudden volatility this week. US stock shield near record

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:58.980
with the S&amp;P 500 at 7,511 down 0.1%. The NASDAQ composite sits at 26,617 down 0.2% while

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:09.080
the TSX composite slipped to 34,299 down 0.3%. Fresh US strikes in Iran drove crude higher and

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:14.780
kept sentiment cautious despite strong earnings from several names. Portfolio year-to-date

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:23.740
return sits at plus 0.42% against the NASDAQ's plus 14.55% year-to-date, leaving alpha at

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:32.160
negative 14.13%. About 15 days ago, picked ACM on an infrastructure contract win that

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:39.980
ultimately closed down 11.35%. A reminder that even multi-year revenue visibility can be swamped

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:45.840
by broader rotation. With markets this jittery, let's see how we're positioning in today's simulated

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:53.680
trade. Snowflake flashed higher on a raised annual revenue forecast and a $6 billion AWS partnership

00:01:53.680 --> 00:02:01.380
deal. The stock gapped 39% pre-market on volume well above recent averages, breaking above the

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:08.300
prior session high with momentum extending into the open. This is a simulated flash trade for educational

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:17.240
purposes only, with a same day hold targeting plus 4% to plus 9% on strength. Mental stops sits 8%

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:23.940
below entry to cap any reversal if broader market rotation hits tech. Confidence is medium because

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:30.180
the strong catalyst and volume alignment are clear, yet single-day gap moves carry reversal risk.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:36.280
The exercise shows how to evaluate an earnings related catalyst with immediate volume confirmation

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:42.480
before entering. Position sizing discipline on high volatility names remains essential regardless

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:48.220
of outcome. Before we check how yesterday's trade played out, here's the lesson we're carrying

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:59.240
forward. Yesterday, we simulated buying TSM at $400 and $27.02 at the open and exited at $422.73.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:10.120
The position lost 1% or $10.05 on a $1,000 stake. The NASDAQ fell roughly 0.4% over the same

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:18.820
window, so the trade produced negative 0.60% alpha. The setup relied on AI visibility but failed to hold

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:25.320
once broader rotation began. The new rule requires volume above the 20-day average before entering

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:31.880
momentum trades on earnings beats. That discipline lesson pairs directly with our strategy spotlight

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:39.100
on inflation protection. TIPS ETFs are seeing inflows as investors seek inflation protection,

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:45.060
yet the underlying mechanism often fails to deliver when real yields shift or supply chains

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:52.180
adjust faster than CPI. The strategy involves buying treasury inflation protected S securities through

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:59.020
ETFs to hedge rising consumer prices. When inflation hits a 3-year height, the funds can still post

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:06.040
negative real returns if break-even rates are mispriced. Implementation requires checking the ETFs

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:10.760
real yield spread versus nominal treasuries on your brokerage platform before allocating.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:19.020
Size the position to no more than 5-8% of the fixed income sleeve. This approach worked best in 2021

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:25.900
to 2022 when inflation surprised to the upside and TIPS outperform nominal bonds by several

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:33.440
percentage points. Always compare the ETFs 30-day SEC yield to the 5-year break-even inflation rate

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:40.000
before purchase. Speaking of sustainable income, our investor education segment tackles dividend

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:46.380
traps. Imagine you bought a Canadian dividend ETF last quarter, expecting steady cash flow

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:53.300
only to watch the payout ratio climb above 80% after an earnings miss. Companies must generate

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:59.000
sufficient free cash flow to cover dividends without eroding the balance sheet. When payout exceeds

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:06.780
70-75% for non-reads, the risk of acute rises sharply even if the headline yield looks attractive.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:12.360
The dividend tax credit in non-registered accounts reduces the effective tax rate

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:20.960
one eligible Canadian dividends to roughly 10-20% depending on your bracket. TFSA and RRSP accounts

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:26.120
eliminate that advantage entirely, so growth-oriented holdings may be better there.

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:33.140
Screen for dividend aristocrats with 10 or more years of increases and payout ratios below 60%

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:37.360
using your broker's fundamentals greener before adding to a TFSA.

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:43.660
The biggest mistake with dividend strategies is chasing the highest yield without checking sustainability.

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:49.260
Instead, always calculate the payout ratio and free cash flow coverage first.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:56.640
Two Canadian tools can help you execute these ideas more efficiently. Wealth symbols tax loss harvesting

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:03.880
tool automatically scans TFSA and non-registered accounts for superficial loss-rule violations and

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:10.120
suggest replacement ETFs within the same sector. Canadian investors can run the scan in under

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:16.300
two minutes before year end with the free tier covering basic accounts. Interactive broker's

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:22.580
option chains API provides real-time bid-ask data and Greeks for covered call strategies directly

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:31.100
in the trader workstation platform. Users can filter 430-45 day expires on TSX names and calculate

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:37.000
annualized yield before placing orders. A few quick hits before we close with your weekly challenge.

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:42.460
Hormel Foods topped quarterly estimates on strong demand for protein-rich foods

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:47.380
with chicken and turkey product demand driving beats on both sales and profit.

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:53.840
Add HRL to a watch list for any post-earnings pullback below the 50-day moving average.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:07:00.580
Cole's stock spiked 20% as comparable sales growth reached the best level in four years despite

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:07.140
overall revenue decline. Consider trimming any existing retail exposure if the spike fails to hold

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:13.640
above the opening gap high. Best Buy beat on top and bottom lines as the company works to reverse its

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:20.260
sales slump through ads and marketplace expansion. Add BBY to a tech watch list for potential sector

00:07:20.260 --> 00:07:27.620
rotation entry on any follow-through volume. Intact financial fell 14%, it remains a long-term

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:34.900
compounder with a history of steady dividend growth. Review IFKT the TSX for a TFSA starter

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:41.000
position if it stabilizes above the recent low. Finally, put today's lessons into action with this

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:47.440
week's listener challenge. Open your brokerage's screener, filter TSX dividend payers for payout

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:55.480
ratios under 60% and 5-year dividend growth above 5%. Then add the top three results to a new watch list

00:07:55.480 --> 00:08:03.020
for next week's review. Before we wrap, watch for how the SNOW Flash Trader resolves by the

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:09.240
close and whether volume sustains above the 20-day average. That's your modern investing techniques

